        "original_id": "8240d9f5-7cb7-5e7e-ad55-2f7aeabfd6be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shanghai, Hengyang, Hunan Province, China\n- People: Ye Sha, Zhu Shaolian\n- Organizations: Communist Youth League of China, Communist Party of China\n- Roles: radio personality\n- Topics: population, urban area, municipal status\n\nFacts:\n- Zhu Shaolian was born in Hengyang, Hunan Province.\n- Zhu Shaolian joined the Communist Youth League of China in 1921.\n- Zhu Shaolian joined the Communist Party of China in February 1922.\n- Hengyang's built-up or metro area, made of 4 of its 5 urban districts, had 1,075,516 inhabitants in the 2010 census.\n- Shanghai had a population of more than 24 million as of 2014.\n- Shanghai is one of the four direct-controlled municipalities of China.\n- Shanghai is the most populous city proper in the world.\n- Ye Sha is a radio personality from Shanghai, China.",
